{
  "reductionName": "Weighted Cut Reduction",
  "reductionDefinition": "Karp\u0027s reduction from Partition to Weighted Cut: each number of S becomes a node, every two nodes are joined by an edge weighing the product of their two numbers, and K is a quarter of the square of the numbers\u0027 total. A split of S into two sides that add up to a and b cuts edges weighing a * b in all, which reaches K only when a = b, so S splits into two halves of equal sum exactly when the graph has a cut weighing at least K.",
  "source": "Karp, Richard M. Reducibility among combinatorial problems. Complexity of computer computations. Springer, Boston, MA, 1972. 85-103.",
  "sourceFile": "Problems/NPComplete/NPC_PARTITION/ReduceTo/NPC_WEIGHTEDCUT/WEIGHTEDCUTReduction.cs",
  "contributors": [
    "Andrija Sevaljevic"
  ],
  "visualization": {
    "visualizationName": "Weighted Cut Visualization",
    "visualizationDefinition": "This is a default visualization for Cut",
    "visualizationType": "GraphD3",
